    "text": "25 Board Games That We All Played in the ’70s and ’80s\nBy Stephen Lenz,\n7 hours agoLong before \"screen time\" and connecting via social media, rainy Saturdays in the 1970s revolved around the thrill of Trouble's Pop-O-Matic bubble, the sound of plastic chips falling from the Connect Four grid or maybe, if you were lucky to survive, the nerve-shredding buzz from a misguided funny bone removal during Operation (there was nothing funny about it).",
